Usage: file [OPTION]... [FILE]...

The file command tests each argument in an attempt to classify it.
There are three sets of tests, performed in this order:
filesystem tests, magic number tests, and language tests.

The first test that succeeds causes the file type to be printed.
On Windows, file type detection is based on file extensions and
attributes (directory, symlink, regular file).

OPTIONS:
  -b, --brief              do not prepend filenames to output lines
  -c, --checking-printout  print the checking format
  -f, --files-from ARG     read the filenames from FILE
  -k, --keep-going         don't stop at first match
  -m, --magic-file ARG     use FILE as magic file
  -h, --no-dereference     don't follow symlinks
  -i, --mime               output MIME type strings
  -L, --dereference        follow symlinks
  -n, --no-buffer          do not buffer output
  -N, --no-pad             do not pad output
  -z, --uncompress         try to decompress compressed files
      --help               display this help and exit
  -V, --version            output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
